# 🏗️ System Architecture

EduPilot 2.0 follows a full-stack client–server architecture that integrates the React frontend, Flask backend, application services, SQLite database, and external APIs.

The following flowchart illustrates the major components and how they interact throughout the learning process.

#### 📊 Architecture Flowchart
```text
flowchart TD
    USER(["👤 Student / User"])

    subgraph FRONTEND["🎨 Frontend — React + Vite"]
        direction TB
        UI["EduPilot User Interface"]
        AUTH["🔐 Login & Registration"]
        DASH["📚 Learning Dashboard"]
        NOTES["📝 AI Notes & Summaries"]
        DOCS["📄 Document Upload & Analysis"]
        QUIZ["🧠 Interactive Quizzes"]
        FLASH["🗂️ Flashcards"]
        CHAT["🤖 AI Study Chatbot"]
        PLAN["📅 Study Planner"]
        ANALYSIS["📊 Learning Analysis"]
        CLIENT["📡 Axios API Client"]

        UI --> AUTH
        UI --> DASH
        DASH --> NOTES
        DASH --> DOCS
        DASH --> QUIZ
        DASH --> FLASH
        DASH --> CHAT
        DASH --> PLAN
        DASH --> ANALYSIS

        AUTH --> CLIENT
        NOTES --> CLIENT
        DOCS --> CLIENT
        QUIZ --> CLIENT
        FLASH --> CLIENT
        CHAT --> CLIENT
        PLAN --> CLIENT
        ANALYSIS --> CLIENT
    end

    subgraph BACKEND["⚙️ Backend — Python + Flask"]
        direction TB
        API["Flask API Routes"]
        VALIDATE["Request Validation"]
        SECURITY["JWT Authentication & Access Control"]
        LOGIC["Application Logic"]

        API --> VALIDATE
        VALIDATE --> SECURITY
        SECURITY --> LOGIC
    end

    subgraph SERVICES["🧩 Learning Services"]
        direction TB
        CONTENT["Content Generation"]
        DOCUMENT["Document Text Extraction"]
        QUIZ_SERVICE["Quiz Processing & Attempt Recording"]
        FLASH_SERVICE["Flashcard Processing & CSV Export"]
        CHAT_SERVICE["AI Chat Processing"]
        PLANNER["Study Plan Management"]
        INSIGHTS["Performance & Topic Analysis"]
        SESSION["Saved Session Management"]
        PDF["PDF Export"]
    end

    subgraph DATABASE["🗄️ Database Layer"]
        ORM["SQLAlchemy ORM"]
        DB[("SQLite Database")]
        USERDATA["User Records"]
        SAVED["Saved Learning Sessions"]
        ATTEMPTS["Quiz Attempts"]
        PLANS["Study Plan Entries"]

        ORM <--> DB
        DB --- USERDATA
        DB --- SAVED
        DB --- ATTEMPTS
        DB --- PLANS
    end

    subgraph EXTERNAL["🌐 External Integrations"]
        GEMINI["Google Gemini API"]
        YOUTUBE["YouTube Data API<br/>Where Configured"]
    end

    USER --> UI
    CLIENT <-->|"HTTP / JSON"| API

    LOGIC --> CONTENT
    LOGIC --> DOCUMENT
    LOGIC --> QUIZ_SERVICE
    LOGIC --> FLASH_SERVICE
    LOGIC --> CHAT_SERVICE
    LOGIC --> PLANNER
    LOGIC --> INSIGHTS
    LOGIC --> SESSION
    LOGIC --> PDF

    DOCUMENT --> CONTENT

    CONTENT <--> GEMINI
    QUIZ_SERVICE <--> GEMINI
    FLASH_SERVICE <--> GEMINI
    CHAT_SERVICE <--> GEMINI
    CONTENT <--> YOUTUBE

    CONTENT <--> ORM
    DOCUMENT <--> ORM
    QUIZ_SERVICE <--> ORM
    PLANNER <--> ORM
    INSIGHTS <--> ORM
    SESSION <--> ORM
```

#### 🔄 Request and Response Flow
```text
flowchart TD
    A(["👤 User Action"])
    B["React Frontend"]
    C["Axios HTTP Request"]
    D["Flask API Endpoint"]
    E["Validate Input & Authentication"]
    F{"Request Valid and Authorized?"}
    G["Return Error Response"]
    H["Execute Application Workflow"]
    I{"External AI Service Required?"}
    J["Call Google Gemini API"]
    K["Process Result"]
    L[("Save or Retrieve Data<br/>SQLite + SQLAlchemy")]
    M["Return API Response"]
    N["Update React Interface"]
    O(["✅ Result Displayed to User"])

    A --> B --> C --> D --> E --> F
    F -- No --> G
    G --> N
    F -- Yes --> H --> I
    I -- Yes --> J --> K
    I -- No --> K
    K --> L --> M --> N --> O
```

#### 🧱 Architecture Components

Layer| Main Responsibilities
🎨 Frontend| User interface, authentication screens, dashboard, notes, summaries, quizzes, flashcards, chatbot, and study planner.
📡 API Communication| Sends frontend requests and receives responses through Axios and HTTP.
⚙️ Backend| Flask routes, input validation, authentication checks, business logic, and coordination of application workflows.
🧠 Learning Services| AI content generation, document processing, quiz handling, flashcards, chatbot requests, study planning, learning analysis, and exports.
🗄️ Database| Persists supported user records, saved sessions, quiz attempts, and study-plan entries using SQLAlchemy and SQLite.
🌐 External APIs| Google Gemini for configured AI features and YouTube Data API where enabled.

Security note: API keys remain on the backend in environment variables. Protected operations should verify authentication and user ownership before accessing private records.

The flowcharts describe the logical architecture. Actual routes, model relationships, and external integrations depend on the current backend implementation.

---

#### Frontend Responsibilities

The React application manages the user interface, user interactions, local component state, navigation, and requests to the backend API.

#### Backend Responsibilities

The Flask application handles API requests, authentication checks, learning workflows, database operations, document processing, and communication with configured external services.

#### Database Responsibilities

SQLite provides persistent storage for supported application records, including users, saved learning sessions, quiz attempts, and study-plan entries.

#### AI Integration

The Google Gemini API is used for configured AI-assisted tasks such as generating learning material, quizzes, or explanations. The exact model and task allocation depend on the current backend configuration.

