## 🗃️ Database Design

EduPilot uses SQLite with SQLAlchemy models.

The known application data areas include:

Data model / area| Purpose
"User"| Stores user account records and password hashes.
"SavedSession"| Stores topic-based or document-based learning sessions and associated generated content.
"QuizAttempt"| Records quiz performance, including topic, score, total questions, percentage, difficulty, answers, and creation time.
"StudyPlanEntry"| Supports scheduled study reviews and their duration settings.

The exact field definitions, relationships, constraints, and initialization process should be confirmed against the final database models in "backend/app.py".

---

## 🔌 API Overview

The Flask backend exposes API endpoints consumed by the React frontend.

The following endpoints have been identified in the shared backend code:

Endpoint| Method| Purpose
"/api/upload-file"| POST| Upload and analyse a supported study document.
"/api/quiz-attempt"| POST| Save a completed quiz attempt for the authenticated user.
"/api/quiz-attempts"| GET| Retrieve quiz attempts for the authenticated user.
"/api/weak-topics"| GET| Analyse recent quiz attempts for weaker and stronger topics.

The frontend also uses operations for topic-based content generation, quiz generation, study-plan management, and chatbot interactions.

Before publication, add the exact route names and HTTP methods for those operations directly from the final "backend/app.py". Do not treat this table as a complete API specification.

