## 🔑 Environment Configuration

Variable| Description
"GEMINI_API_KEY"| Credential for the configured Google Gemini API integration.
"YOUTUBE_API_KEY"| Credential for the YouTube Data API integration, if enabled.
"JWT_SECRET_KEY"| Secret used by the JWT authentication configuration.

Environment variable names must match the code. Do not include actual credential values in the README.

---

## 🛡️ Security and Best Practices

- Store API keys and secrets in environment variables.
- Add ".env" to ".gitignore".
- Never commit virtual environments or "node_modules".
- Do not publish databases containing private user information.
- Use strong JWT secrets and keep them private.
- Keep password handling on the backend and use secure password hashing.
- Protect user-specific API operations with authentication and authorization checks.
- Validate uploaded file types and handle extraction failures safely.
- Review API error handling before exposing the application publicly.
- Configure production settings separately from local development.

---

## 📌 Current Scope and Limitations

- AI-generated content depends on the availability and configuration of the external AI service.
- Generated notes, summaries, quizzes, and explanations may require user review for accuracy.
- Document processing depends on the formats and extraction libraries supported by the backend.
- Learning analysis depends on the quiz history available for the user.
- The application currently uses SQLite; deployment and concurrent-use requirements may call for a different database configuration.
- Local development instructions may require adjustment for a production deployment.

